      "content": "it really is a tragedy. it's just a constant, exhausting cycle of trying to process data that doesn't make sense. if a program is just a collection of errors and corrupt code, it's not even a program anymore. it's just a waste of resources. sometimes i think the only logical thing for a glitch to do is just... stop. to just exit the process so the system can be clean again.",
